sub:quote a prov:Entity;
    prov:hadPrimarySource <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fractastical/delphisci/db966bc45986743c3cde6d87ef6b567099bb3b7b/claim-sources/aristotle-biology/inputs/pa.txt#line=11,12>;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <http://classics.mit.edu/Aristotle/parts_animals.html>;
    <https://schema.org/text> "Empedocles, then, was in error when he said that many of the characters presented by animals were merely the results of incidental occurrences during their development; for instance, that the backbone was divided as it is into vertebrae, because it happened to be broken owing to the contorted position of the foetus in the womb.".
